Typed `Session` / `Reference` / `Argument` over the pancake archives
([`lib.rs`](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/bindings/rust/src/lib.rs)).
Cargo features select transports (`tcp` / `inproc` default; `iroh` opt-in).
Install: [Bindings]($link.page('bindings')).

## The same round-trip

The [Start building]($link.page('start')) round-trip (connect, fetch, send,
handle the reply) reads like this in Rust. The snippet uses the crate's opt-in
`async` feature and runs inside a `tokio::task::LocalSet`. Unlike TS/Python,
`connect` already starts the inbound loop; call `Session::serve` only when you
want to await shutdown.

> []($block.attrs('code-tabs'))
> **tcp**
> ```rust
> use pancake::{connect, tcp_locator, Argument};
>
> // tcp: the peer is a place, a cleartext host and port.
> let partner = tcp_locator("127.0.0.1", 9099);
>
> let session = connect(&partner, None, None).await?;
> let greeter = session.fetch("greeter").await?; // a capability, by name
> match session
>     .send(&greeter, "greet", &[Argument::String("world".into())])
>     .await
> {
>     Ok(Argument::String(reply)) => println!("{reply}"),
>     Ok(other) => println!("unexpected reply: {other:?}"),
>     Err(reason) => eprintln!("the greeter refused: {reason:?}"),
> }
> session.close();
> ```
> **iroh**
> ```rust
> // Cargo.toml: pancake = { …, features = ["iroh"] }
> use pancake::{connect, Argument, Reachability};
>
> // iroh reachability: the peer is a key, not a place. Discovery resolves
> // the bare node id over the open internet; no address in hand.
> let partner = "ocapn://3b6a…da29.iroh";
>
> let session = connect(partner, Some(Reachability::Discovery), None).await?;
> let greeter = session.fetch("greeter").await?; // a capability, by name
> match session
>     .send(&greeter, "greet", &[Argument::String("world".into())])
>     .await
> {
>     Ok(Argument::String(reply)) => println!("{reply}"),
>     Ok(other) => println!("unexpected reply: {other:?}"),
>     Err(reason) => eprintln!("the greeter refused: {reason:?}"),
> }
> session.close();
> ```

Iroh needs the `iroh` Cargo feature and a bare node id; fetch/send match the
tcp tab. Dial-by-id: [iroh]($link.page('transports/iroh')). CapTP ideas:
[Concepts]($link.page('concepts')).

## Async

[tokio](https://tokio.rs/) behind an opt-in `async` feature. Handles are
`!Send`: one task inside a `LocalSet`. Host calls stay synchronous; only socket
I/O awaits. Hosting the other half: rooms client linked below, or Zig
[Start]($link.page('start')).

## Actors

`session.spawn` / `session.publish` take a `FnMut(&str, &[Argument])` closure.
A panic settles the answer broken without crossing the C boundary. Pipelining
and attenuation: [Concepts]($link.page('concepts')).

## Binding check and example

```sh
zig build rust-dogfood    # cargo test against the pancake archives, sync + async
```

The full surface lives in the
[Rust binding README](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/bindings/rust/README.md),
and the
[rooms chat client](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/apps/rooms/rust/client.rs)
builds a small capability-secure room on this surface.
